      "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(0)y(0)+x(-1)y(-1)+x(2)y(2).\n$$\n\nFind $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx(t)=3+t-2{t}^{2},\\,y(t)=t-3.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(0)y(0)+x(-1)y(-1)+x(2)y(2) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot (-4)+(-3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-9+0+3 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
